      "worked": "The parallel line has gradient $-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=3x^2-4\\\\3x^2-4&=-1\\\\x^2&=1\\\\x&=\\pm1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe contact points are $(1,-3)$ and $(-1,3)$. Using $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$ at each point,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y+3&=-(x-1)\\\\y&=-x-2,\\\\y-3&=-(x+1)\\\\y&=-x+2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
